    "title": "<p class=\"TableTitle\"><strong>Table&nbsp;6.02</strong> Histological criteria for grading appendiceal mucinous neoplasms and their peritoneal metastases</p>",
    "legend": "",
    "source": "Reetesh K. Pai",
    "copyright": "",
    "tablehtml": "<table class=\"MsoNormalTable\" style=\"width: 100.0%; border-collapse: collapse; mso-yfti-tbllook: 1184; mso-padding-alt: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" border=\"0\" width=\"100%\" cellspacing=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\">\r\n<tbody>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 0; mso-yfti-firstrow: yes; page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 25.0%; border: none; border-top: solid windowtext 1.0pt; mso-border-top-alt: solid windowtext .5pt; background: #8DB3E2; mso-background-themecolor: text2; mso-background-themetint: 102; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"25%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Primary appendiceal tumour</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 25.0%; border: none; border-top: solid windowtext 1.0pt; mso-border-top-alt: solid windowtext .5pt; background: #8DB3E2; mso-background-themecolor: text2; mso-background-themetint: 102; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"25%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"mso-bookmark: _Hlk210039846;\"><strong><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Histological criteria in the primary tumour</span></strong></span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 25.0%; border: none; border-top: solid windowtext 1.0pt; mso-border-top-alt: solid windowtext .5pt; background: #8DB3E2; mso-background-themecolor: text2; mso-background-themetint: 102; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"25%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"mso-bookmark: _Hlk210039846;\"><strong><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Terminology for potential peritoneal metastasis</span></strong></span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 25.0%; border: none; border-top: solid windowtext 1.0pt; mso-border-top-alt: solid windowtext .5pt; background: #8DB3E2; mso-background-themecolor: text2; mso-background-themetint: 102; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"25%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"mso-bookmark: _Hlk210039846;\"><strong><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Grading criteria for peritoneal metastases<sup>a</sup></span></strong></span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 1; page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 25.0%; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"25%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"mso-bookmark: _Hlk210039846;\">Low-grade appendiceal mucinous neoplasm</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 25.0%; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"25%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"mso-bookmark: _Hlk210039846;\">Circumferential proliferation of mucinous epithelium with low-grade cytological features and pushing, diverticulum-like extension into or through the wall</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 25.0%; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"25%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"mso-bookmark: _Hlk210039846;\">Low-grade mucinous carcinoma peritonei</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 25.0%; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"25%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"mso-bookmark: _Hlk210039846;\">Hypocellular mucinous deposits</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"mso-bookmark: _Hlk210039846;\">Strips of neoplastic epithelium with low-grade cytological features</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"mso-bookmark: _Hlk210039846;\">No infiltrative-type invasion by small glands, mucin pools, or signet-ring cells</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 2; page-break-inside: avoid; height: 98.3pt;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 25.0%; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 98.3pt;\" rowspan=\"2\" valign=\"top\" width=\"25%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"mso-bookmark: _Hlk210039846;\"><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">High-grade appendiceal mucinous neoplasm</span></span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 25.0%; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 98.3pt;\" rowspan=\"2\" valign=\"top\" width=\"25%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"mso-bookmark: _Hlk210039846;\"><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Circumferential proliferation of mucinous epithelium with high-grade cytological features and pushing, diverticulum-like extension into or through the wall</span></span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 25.0%; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 98.3pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"25%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"mso-bookmark: _Hlk210039846;\"><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">High-grade mucinous carcinoma peritonei</span></span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 25.0%; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 98.3pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"25%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"mso-bookmark: _Hlk210039846;\"><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Hypercellular mucinous deposits as judged at 20&times; magnification</span></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"mso-bookmark: _Hlk210039846;\"><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Strips and clusters of neoplastic epithelium with high-grade cytological features (&ge;&nbsp;10% of tumour epithelium)</span></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"mso-bookmark: _Hlk210039846;\"><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Foci of infiltrative-type invasion by angulated glands in a desmoplastic stroma, or numerous small mucin pools containing clusters of tumour cells</span></span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 3; mso-yfti-lastrow: yes; page-break-inside: avoid; height: 98.3pt;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 25.0%; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 98.3pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"25%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"mso-bookmark: _Hlk210039846;\"><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">High-grade mucinous carcinoma peritonei with signet-ring cells</span></span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 25.0%; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 98.3pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"25%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"mso-bookmark: _Hlk210039846;\"><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Infiltrative signet-ring cells with desmoplasia or single cells floating in mucin pools<sup>b</sup></span></span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</tbody>\r\n</table>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><sup>a</sup>Generally, the grade of the tumour in the appendix is concordant with that of the peritoneum. The grade of the peritoneal tumour has a greater effect on prognosis than that of the appendiceal primary tumour in discordant cases. <sup>b</sup>At least 10% of the tumour should be signet-ring cells for this designation. Signet-ring cells in mucin must be distinguished from degenerate tumour cells (pseudo&ndash;signet-ring cells) in the mucin.</p>",
    "imageUrl": null,
    "thumbnail": null
  },
  {
    "pkattachmentId": 74867,
    "bookid": 72,
    "chapterId": 52,
    "fileId": 48725,
    "type": "WSI",
    "diagnosis": "Low-grade appendiceal mucinous neoplasm",
    "title": "",
    "legend": "The tumor shows broad-front diverticulum-like invasion in the appendiceal wall. Neoplastic epithelium has an undulating appearance but true crypt formation is lacking. The tumor cells are neoplastic with enlarged, hyperchromatic nuclei and apoptotic debris with occasional mitotic figures.",
    "source": "Rhonda K. Yantiss",
    "copyright": "",
    "tablehtml": "",
    "imageUrl": "https://tumourclassification.iarc.who.int/static/dzi/48725.dzi",
    "thumbnail": null
  },
